@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.1905 = private unnamed_addr constant [722 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks that async functions do not contain blocking HTTP calls.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ABlocking an async function via a blocking HTTP call will block the entire\0Aevent loop, preventing it from executing other tasks while waiting for the\0AHTTP response, negating the benefits of asynchronous programming.\0A\0AInstead of making a blocking HTTP call, use an asynchronous HTTP client\0Alibrary such as `aiohttp` or `httpx`.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aasync def fetch():\0A    urllib.request.urlopen(\22https://example.com/foo/bar\22).read()\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aasync def fetch():\0A    async with aiohttp.ClientSession() as session:\0A        async with session.get(\22https://example.com/foo/bar\22) as resp:\0A            ...\0A```\0A", align 1
