@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.1917 = private unnamed_addr constant [528 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for insecure `logging.config.listen` calls.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A`logging.config.listen` starts a server that listens for logging\0Aconfiguration requests. This is insecure, as parts of the configuration are\0Apassed to the built-in `eval` function, which can be used to execute\0Aarbitrary code.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport logging\0A\0Alogging.config.listen(9999)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `logging.config.listen()`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/logging.config.html#logging.config.listen)\0A", align 1
