@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.1920 = private unnamed_addr constant [366 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for calls to `ssl.wrap_socket()` without an `ssl_version`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThis method is known to provide a default value that maximizes\0Acompatibility, but permits use of insecure protocols.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport ssl\0A\0Assl.wrap_socket()\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport ssl\0A\0Assl.wrap_socket(ssl_version=ssl.PROTOCOL_TLSv1_2)\0A```\0A", align 1
