@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.1939 = private unnamed_addr constant [577 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for loop control variables that override the loop iterable.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ALoop control variables should not override the loop iterable, as this can\0Alead to confusing behavior.\0A\0AInstead, use a distinct variable name for any loop control variables.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aitems = [1, 2, 3]\0A\0Afor items in items:\0A    print(items)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aitems = [1, 2, 3]\0A\0Afor item in items:\0A    print(item)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: The `for` statement](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/compound_stmts.html#the-for-statement)\0A", align 1
