@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.1965 = private unnamed_addr constant [2965 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for methods that use custom [`TypeVar`s][typing_TypeVar] in their\0Aannotations when they could use [`Self`][Self] instead.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AWhile the semantics are often identical, using `Self` is more intuitive\0Aand succinct (per [PEP 673]) than a custom `TypeVar`. For example, the\0Ause of `Self` will typically allow for the omission of type parameters\0Aon the `self` and `cls` arguments.\0A\0AThis check currently applies to instance methods that return `self`,\0Aclass methods that return an instance of `cls`, class methods that return\0A`cls`, and `__new__` methods.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```pyi\0Afrom typing import TypeVar\0A\0A_S = TypeVar(\22_S\22, bound=\22Foo\22)\0A\0Aclass Foo:\0A    def __new__(cls: type[_S], *args: str, **kwargs: int) -> _S: ...\0A    def foo(self: _S, arg: bytes) -> _S: ...\0A    @classmethod\0A    def bar(cls: type[_S], arg: int) -> _S: ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```pyi\0Afrom typing import Self\0A\0Aclass Foo:\0A    def __new__(cls, *args: str, **kwargs: int) -> Self: ...\0A    def foo(self, arg: bytes) -> Self: ...\0A    @classmethod\0A    def bar(cls, arg: int) -> Self: ...\0A```\0A\0A## Fix behaviour and safety\0AThe fix replaces all references to the custom type variable in the method's header and body\0Awith references to `Self`. The fix also adds an import of `Self` if neither `Self` nor `typing`\0Ais already imported in the module. If your [`target-version`] setting is set to Python 3.11 or\0Anewer, the fix imports `Self` from the standard-library `typing` module; otherwise, the fix\0Aimports `Self` from the third-party [`typing_extensions`][typing_extensions] backport package.\0A\0AIf the custom type variable is a [PEP-695]-style `TypeVar`, the fix also removes the `TypeVar`\0Adeclaration from the method's [type parameter list]. However, if the type variable is an\0Aold-style `TypeVar`, the declaration of the type variable will not be removed by this rule's\0Afix, as the type variable could still be used by other functions, methods or classes. See\0A[`unused-private-type-var`][PYI018] for a rule that will clean up unused private type\0Avariables.\0A\0AThe fix is only marked as unsafe if there is the possibility that it might delete a comment\0Afrom your code.\0A\0A## Availability\0A\0ABecause this rule relies on the third-party `typing_extensions` module for Python versions\0Abefore 3.11, its diagnostic will not be emitted, and no fix will be offered, if\0A`typing_extensions` imports have been disabled by the [`lint.typing-extensions`] linter option.\0A\0A## Options\0A\0A- `lint.typing-extensions`\0A\0A[PEP 673]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0673/#motivation\0A[PEP-695]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0695/\0A[PYI018]: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/unused-private-type-var/\0A[type parameter list]: https://docs.python.org/3/reference/compound_stmts.html#type-params\0A[Self]: https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.Self\0A[typing_TypeVar]: https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.TypeVar\0A[typing_extensions]: https://typing-extensions.readthedocs.io/en/latest/\0A", align 1
