@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.1970 = private unnamed_addr constant [648 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for incorrect function signatures on `__exit__` and `__aexit__`\0Amethods.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AImproperly annotated `__exit__` and `__aexit__` methods can cause\0Aunexpected behavior when interacting with type checkers.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```pyi\0Afrom types import TracebackType\0A\0Aclass Foo:\0A    def __exit__(\0A        self, typ: BaseException, exc: BaseException, tb: TracebackType\0A    ) -> None: ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```pyi\0Afrom types import TracebackType\0A\0Aclass Foo:\0A    def __exit__(\0A        self,\0A        typ: type[BaseException] | None,\0A        exc: BaseException | None,\0A        tb: TracebackType | None,\0A    ) -> None: ...\0A```\0A", align 1
