@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2009 = private unnamed_addr constant [1016 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for untyped function arguments in stubs with default values that\0Aare not \22simple\22 /// (i.e., `int`, `float`, `complex`, `bytes`, `str`,\0A`bool`, `None`, `...`, or simple container literals).\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AStub (`.pyi`) files exist to define type hints, and are not evaluated at\0Aruntime. As such, function arguments in stub files should not have default\0Avalues, as they are ignored by type checkers.\0A\0AHowever, the use of default values may be useful for IDEs and other\0Aconsumers of stub files, and so \22simple\22 values may be worth including and\0Aare permitted by this rule.\0A\0AInstead of including and reproducing a complex value, use `...` to indicate\0Athat the assignment has a default value, but that the value is non-simple\0Aor varies according to the current platform or Python version.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```pyi\0Adef foo(arg=[]) -> None: ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```pyi\0Adef foo(arg=...) -> None: ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [`flake8-pyi`](https://github.com/PyCQA/flake8-pyi/blob/main/ERRORCODES.md)\0A", align 1
