@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2012 = private unnamed_addr constant [953 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for assignments in stubs with default values that are not \22simple\22\0A(i.e., `int`, `float`, `complex`, `bytes`, `str`, `bool`, `None`, `...`, or\0Asimple container literals).\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AStub (`.pyi`) files exist to define type hints, and are not evaluated at\0Aruntime. As such, assignments in stub files should not include values,\0Aas they are ignored by type checkers.\0A\0AHowever, the use of such values may be useful for IDEs and other consumers\0Aof stub files, and so \22simple\22 values may be worth including and are\0Apermitted by this rule.\0A\0AInstead of including and reproducing a complex value, use `...` to indicate\0Athat the assignment has a default value, but that the value is non-simple\0Aor varies according to the current platform or Python version.\0A\0A## Example\0A```pyi\0Afoo: str = \22...\22\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```pyi\0Afoo: str = ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [`flake8-pyi`](https://github.com/PyCQA/flake8-pyi/blob/main/ERRORCODES.md)\0A", align 1
