@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2172 = private unnamed_addr constant [1205 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `pd.merge` on Pandas objects.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIn Pandas, the `.merge` method (exposed on, e.g., `DataFrame` objects) and\0Athe `pd.merge` function (exposed on the Pandas module) are equivalent.\0A\0AFor consistency, prefer calling `.merge` on an object over calling\0A`pd.merge` on the Pandas module, as the former is more idiomatic.\0A\0AFurther, `pd.merge` is not a method, but a function, which prohibits it\0Afrom being used in method chains, a common pattern in Pandas code.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport pandas as pd\0A\0Acats_df = pd.read_csv(\22cats.csv\22)\0Adogs_df = pd.read_csv(\22dogs.csv\22)\0Arabbits_df = pd.read_csv(\22rabbits.csv\22)\0Apets_df = pd.merge(pd.merge(cats_df, dogs_df), rabbits_df)  # Hard to read.\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport pandas as pd\0A\0Acats_df = pd.read_csv(\22cats.csv\22)\0Adogs_df = pd.read_csv(\22dogs.csv\22)\0Arabbits_df = pd.read_csv(\22rabbits.csv\22)\0Apets_df = cats_df.merge(dogs_df).merge(rabbits_df)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Pandas documentation: `merge`](https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/reference/api/pandas.DataFrame.merge.html#pandas.DataFrame.merge)\0A- [Pandas documentation: `pd.merge`](https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/reference/api/pandas.merge.html#pandas.merge)\0A", align 1
