@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2181 = private unnamed_addr constant [786 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for comparisons to `None` which are not using the `is` operator.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AAccording to [PEP 8], \22Comparisons to singletons like None should always be done with\0A`is` or `is not`, never the equality operators.\22\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aif arg != None:\0A    pass\0Aif None == arg:\0A    pass\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aif arg is not None:\0A    pass\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0A\0AThis rule's fix is marked as unsafe, as it may alter runtime behavior when\0Aused with libraries that override the `==`/`__eq__` or `!=`/`__ne__` operators.\0AIn these cases, `is`/`is not` may not be equivalent to `==`/`!=`. For more\0Ainformation, see [this issue].\0A\0A[PEP 8]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/#programming-recommendations\0A[this issue]: https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/4560\0A", align 1
