@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2242 = private unnamed_addr constant [1109 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for functions or methods with too many return statements.\0A\0ABy default, this rule allows up to six return statements, as configured by\0Athe [`lint.pylint.max-returns`] option.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AFunctions or methods with many return statements are harder to understand\0Aand maintain, and often indicative of complex logic.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef capital(country: str) -> str | None:\0A    if country == \22England\22:\0A        return \22London\22\0A    elif country == \22France\22:\0A        return \22Paris\22\0A    elif country == \22Poland\22:\0A        return \22Warsaw\22\0A    elif country == \22Romania\22:\0A        return \22Bucharest\22\0A    elif country == \22Spain\22:\0A        return \22Madrid\22\0A    elif country == \22Thailand\22:\0A        return \22Bangkok\22\0A    else:\0A        return None\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef capital(country: str) -> str | None:\0A    capitals = {\0A        \22England\22: \22London\22,\0A        \22France\22: \22Paris\22,\0A        \22Poland\22: \22Warsaw\22,\0A        \22Romania\22: \22Bucharest\22,\0A        \22Spain\22: \22Madrid\22,\0A        \22Thailand\22: \22Bangkok\22,\0A    }\0A    return capitals.get(country)\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.pylint.max-returns`\0A", align 1
